# Flutter Monorepo — Logging & Error Handling

## Logging — use AppLogger only

```dart
import 'package:logger/logger.dart';

// ✅ correct
final logger = AppLogger(minLevel: LogLevel.debug);
logger.info('User signed in — userId: ${user.id}');
logger.warning('Cache miss');
logger.error('Request failed', exception, stackTrace);

// ❌ never
print('...');
debugPrint('...');
```

Rules:
- Include meaningful context (what, where, relevant IDs).
- Never log passwords, tokens, PII, or raw response bodies.
- Release builds: set minLevel to LogLevel.info or higher.
- Level guide: debug=noise / info=lifecycle / warning=degraded / error=failure / fatal=crash

## Error handling — use Result<T>

```dart
import 'package:core/core.dart';

// ✅ correct — at service/repository boundaries
Future<Result<User>> fetchUser(String id) async {
  try {
    return Success(User.fromJson(await _api.getUser(id)));
  } catch (e, st) {
    _logger.error('fetchUser failed', e, st);
    return Failure(e);
  }
}

// Caller uses pattern matching
switch (await fetchUser(id)) {
  case Success(:final value): showUser(value);
  case Failure(:final error): showError(error);
}

// ❌ wrong — throws across feature boundaries
Future<User> fetchUser(String id) async =>
    User.fromJson(await _api.getUser(id));
```
